Subject: [PATCH] Fil-C port for shadow: always use shadow's own gshadow API

The fil-c musl pizfix has no gshadow API (no <gshadow.h>, no getsgent
family), but the OE target sysroot still carries glibc's <gshadow.h> via
the toolchain's -idirafter, so shadow's __has_include(<gshadow.h>)
guards select glibc's declarations and compile out shadow's own
implementations, leaving pizlonated_*sgent references undefined at link.
Force the guards off so shadow always uses its own gshadow code.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN a/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.c b/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.c
--- a/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.c	2025-12-15 13:15:32.213315030 +0200
+++ b/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.c	2026-11-01 10:04:54.590182457 +0200
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 #include "shadow/gshadow/gshadow.h"
 
 
-#if defined(SHADOWGRP) && !__has_include(<gshadow.h>)
+#if defined(SHADOWGRP) && !0
 // end-working-with shadow group entries
 void
 endsgent(void)
diff -ruN a/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.h b/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.h
--- a/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.h	2025-12-15 13:15:32.213384959 +0200
+++ b/lib/shadow/gshadow/endsgent.h	2026-11-01 10:04:54.533558638 +0200
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 
 
-#if __has_include(<gshadow.h>)
+#if 0
 # include <gshadow.h>
 #else
 void endsgent(void);
